WEBVTT

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:11.220
The history of gaming extends 5,000 
years into the past to ancient Egypt.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:15.720
Ancient games foretold the 
futures of men and kings.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:19.200
They were magic ceremonies that 
determined a person's fate.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.340
These ceremonies were known 
as the "Shadow Games."

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.990
In the present, a young boy 
solves the Millennium Puzzle.

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:30.210
He becomes the heir to the Shadow Games.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:38.300
This boy possesses two hearts - 
one of light and one of darkness.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:42.210
He is known as "Yu-Gi-Oh."

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:50.340
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:57.250
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:04.000
Game cartridges are stacked 
in the corner of the room

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:10.700
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:15.800
You're on the other side of the table

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:19.170
I'm talking to you, but...

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:26.100
You don't change your 
facial expression at all

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:32.350
Even though I'm this close to you

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:39.620
These feelings don't reach 
you, don't reach you

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:46.360
What is truly precious?

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:55.940
Kairyu-Shin

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.650
I might be really skilled!

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:11.460
Jonouchi can't stop grinning.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.320
Of course he's happy.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.280
He defeated Mai Kujaku in his first duel.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:19.280
I can hardly believe it myself.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:22.960
Jonouchi, keep it up and win the next duel.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:24.270
Yeah!

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:27.600
But I sure am hungry.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:30.380
Do you have any food?

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:31.790
Nope.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:39.740
We've come this far from home and 
no one remembers to bring any food?

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:41.280
That is a problem.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.560
This game lasts for two full days.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:47.400
We can't go that long without food or drink.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:51.880
The sponsors of this event should've 
provide food for everybody!

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.700
They're so cheap!

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:56.630
Oh wait!  I have the perfect thing!

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:59.910
Ta-daa!  It's my survival book.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:01.060
What's that?

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:05.420
As a last resort, we can use this 
to find edible weeds and mushrooms.

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:06.800
What?

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:10.330
You idiot!  That's too dangerous to eat!

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:13.450
I smell something good.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:16.310
It's coming from over there.  Let's go!

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:18.410
Food!

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:20.020
Do you smell anything?

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:21.800
You saw his duel against Mai Kujaku.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:24.420
He has the nose of a bloodhound.

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:31.380
I found food!

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:32.740
You sure did.

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:34.330
We're so lucky!

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:38.390
Knock it off!  They belong to someone else!

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:42.830
I'm sure God put it here for us.

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:47.900
What kind of explanation is that?

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:50.890
I think Jonouchi has a point.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:53.910
Save some for me!

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.500
This smells great!

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:01.120
Hot!  Hot!

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:07.470
Chow time!

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:10.430
How dare you!

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:13.200
How dare you steal my fish-

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.670
What was that?

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:23.300
Let's try that one more time.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.800
Oh no, he caught us.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:29.870
How dare you eat my fish!

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:32.180
We didn't eat it yet.

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:34.890
No excuses, you fish thieves!

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:38.100
If you didn't eat it, then 
give me back my fish!

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.590
Star Chips.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:44.910
Are you Ryota Kajiki, the guy who took 
third place at the national championships?

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:47.280
Yes I am.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:49.300
No way!  You're not a castaway?

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.140
I am not a castaway!

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:56.230
I'm Ryota Kajiki, duelist of the wild seas!

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:00.420
What's so funny?

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:01.580
The octopus.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:08.910
Get off of me!

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:10.860
The octopus!

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:13.030
We could've eaten that!

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:17.350
I can't believe they picked duelists 
like you for this tournament.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:20.870
I'm Yugi Muto.  Nice to meet you.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:25.920
You're the Yugi Muto who defeated Kaiba?

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:28.440
That's pretty impressive.

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:31.650
That means you're one of the favorites 
for winning this tournament.

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:33.260
I wouldn't say that.

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:38.340
I'm sorry.  If I'd known it was Yugi and his 
friends, I would've shown more hospitality.

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:39.580
Eat as much as you want.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:40.580
Really?

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:41.510
Sure.

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:44.230
Chow time!

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:49.730
Nothing beats having friends.

00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:51.500
It all worked out.

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:52.430
Yeah.

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:56.140
I'm stuffed.

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:59.010
Cooking freshly caught fish is delicious.

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:02.570
When I win and get the money prize,

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:05.580
I'll buy a big ship and catch 
even more delicious fish.

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:09.100
Your goal is to buy a ship?

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:16.060
Yeah.  I want one of the newest 
models and head back into the ocean.

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:18.870
I'll catch a lot of fish every day!

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:21.840
The ocean sounds nice.

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:25.050
I admire that lifestyle.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:26.900
The ocean is great.

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:29.800
I've been close to the 
ocean since I was born.

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:34.050
I can tell when the ocean 
is happy or when it's upset.

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:37.470
I know everything about the ocean.

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:40.960
Sorry to bore you.

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:42.700
It wasn't boring.

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:45.280
And you let us eat for free.

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:48.050
We'd better get going.

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:50.620
So you're leaving.

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:51.820
Thanks again for the food.

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:53.470
Let's both do our best.

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:00.630
Stop, Yugi!

00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:11.980
I have no business with that weakling, 
but I won't let you escape, Yugi.

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:13.140
How dare you!

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:17.940
I'm not so dumb that I'd let my 
prey nibble on my bait and escape.

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:19.420
Bait?

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:21.920
This area is my turf.

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:25.750
I wait here for duelists to feed on my bait.

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:28.290
Because I have the advantage in the ocean.

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:31.940
Damn, he's treating us like fish.

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:35.030
I knew he was too nice.

00:07:35.030 --> 00:07:40.270
I reeled in my first duelist just awhile 
ago, but he wasn't much of a challenge.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:43.750
Let's duel, Yugi!  I'll defeat you!

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:51.880
Fine.  I accept this duel.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:01.390
This is the Duel Ring for this area.

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:14.590
I'm on the Umi ocean field, and 
you're on the Wasteland field.

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:16.550
Are you okay with that?

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:19.060
Yeah, that's okay.

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:21.790
We'll both wager two Stars.

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:23.030
Fine.

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:29.500
Yugi, this is my territory, 
and you're caught in my net.

00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:31.360
Let's begin the duel!

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:36.490
Yugi, you can do it!

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:38.860
Don't lose to that merman!

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:42.470
I play this card!

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:47.430
What?

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:54.250
My screen isn't showing any data, 
and the monster didn't appear.

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:56.180
What's going on?

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:57.800
What will you do?

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:00.470
My monster is in attack position.

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:05.990
I have to battle an enemy that I can't see?

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:10.580
What's wrong?  It's your turn.

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:13.720
I get it.  His monster did materialize.

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:17.600
There's no data because 
it's hiding underwater.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:23.450
The Umi Field Power Source 
increases Fiend Kraken's power

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:27.650
to 1560 attack points 
and 1820 defense points.

00:09:28.190 --> 00:09:32.910
But you don't understand 
how dangerous the ocean is.

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:35.860
Damn!  Yugi can't attack!

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:37.020
Oh no!

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:38.870
This is unfair, Kajiki!

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:44.940
If this is enough to surprise you, that 
means you're not as good as they say.

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:47.170
I'll just wait and see what happens.

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:50.370
I play this card!

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:58.510
Go, Fiend Kraken!

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:07.270
What?

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:09.510
What is that?

00:10:30.620 --> 00:10:32.440
Tentacle Submission!

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:38.050
Horn Imp is destroyed!

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:43.150
At this rate, Yugi won't 
be able to do anything.

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:48.750
It hid underwater again.

00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:53.270
This is my Sea Stealth Attack!

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:56.300
Sea Stealth Attack?

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:58.920
The true danger of the ocean 
is only getting started.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:01.380
Place your next victim on the field.

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:04.540
If I can't see my enemy,

00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:07.420
I can only place a card in defense 
position and try to survive.

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:09.680
Feral Imp!

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:15.980
But I won't just stand here and do nothing.

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:19.150
I'll show you what I can do next turn.

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:22.310
I know what you're planning.

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:26.980
This is my next card.

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:29.740
Jellyfish!

00:11:30.260 --> 00:11:32.510
I play it in defense position.

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:37.480
It's another enemy I can't see!

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:41.680
What will you do now, Yugi?

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:44.780
I'll play a combo!

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:46.820
Horn of the Unicorn!

00:11:56.030 --> 00:11:57.020
I get it!

00:11:57.020 --> 00:11:58.430
What?

00:11:58.430 --> 00:12:00.870
Even though his enemies are 
hiding in the Umi field,

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:04.040
they're all Water Attribute monsters.

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:09.040
Yugi is going to electrify the Umi ocean.

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:11.640
I see!  I didn't think of that!

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:13.980
Feral Imp, attack!

00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:19.990
He did it!

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:29.910
Why didn't his life points decrease?

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:33.370
You fell for it, Yugi!

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:34.600
What?

00:12:34.820 --> 00:12:39.300
My Jellyfish absorbs electricity!

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:41.600
With this monster on the field,

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:46.710
my Water Attribute monsters are no 
longer weak against electricity.

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:52.500
It's my turn.

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:55.720
Fiend Kraken, attack!

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:01.990
Tentacle Submission!

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:10.700
I'm invincible in the ocean!

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:13.240
Ryota Kajiki is tough.

00:13:13.240 --> 00:13:15.640
His offense and defense have no weaknesses.

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:21.580
Is there a way to destroy this 
bottomless ocean fortress?

00:13:21.580 --> 00:13:25.710
I have to strike him with a hard blow.

00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:27.530
I play this next.

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:29.050
Silver Fang!

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:32.910
Then Full Moon makes it ferocious!

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:42.400
You can't conquer the ocean with that card.

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:46.820
I'll show you how dangerous the ocean is.

00:13:46.820 --> 00:13:49.390
Kairyu-Shin!

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:52.950
What?

00:13:58.280 --> 00:13:59.990
What is that thing?

00:14:00.220 --> 00:14:04.760
The Umi Field Power raises 
its strength to a whopping

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:07.990
2340 attack points and 1950 defense points.

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:10.230
Kairyu-Shin?

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:12.440
Don't underestimate the ocean!

00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:16.030
When you anger the seas, you get punished!

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:19.100
Silver Fang is sunk!

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:27.780
Destroying your monster wasn't 
the only purpose for that attack.

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:28.860
What?

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:31.720
Look at the field.

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:33.070
What's this?

00:14:35.590 --> 00:14:39.020
My field has almost 
completely turned into Umi!

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:42.840
This is Kairyu-Shin's rage.

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:47.860
That attack transformed 
95% of the field into Umi.

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:54.510
Since you can't place any more cards 
on the field, you'll definitely lose.

00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:58.880
My enemies are not only his 
monsters, but the ocean as well.

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:03.440
I can see in your eyes how 
scared you are of the ocean.

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:05.770
Just like how I was in the past.

00:15:05.770 --> 00:15:07.290
What do you mean?

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:11.710
My dad was the best fisherman in my village.

00:15:11.710 --> 00:15:15.390
But I lost my dad to the seas.

00:15:16.300 --> 00:15:21.290
I used to believe that the ocean 
was kind and granted us gifts...

00:15:21.910 --> 00:15:23.370
until that day.

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:27.380
Ryota, the ocean is a monster.

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:28.540
Monster?

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:31.100
Never underestimate the ocean.

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:31.950
Okay.

00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:36.030
The peaceful day suddenly changed.

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:39.270
The ocean suddenly bared its fangs.

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:41.990
Dad!  Look at that!

00:15:43.890 --> 00:15:47.420
Ryota, you'll die if you're thrown overboard.

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:48.790
Dad!

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:58.240
The next thing I knew, the boat 
had drifted back to shore,

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:01.950
but my dad was nowhere to be seen.

00:16:02.780 --> 00:16:04.160
Do you understand, Yugi?

00:16:04.160 --> 00:16:08.140
I have to take my dad's place 
and battle the ocean myself!

00:16:08.140 --> 00:16:13.280
And someday, I'll become Japan's greatest 
fisherman who can survive any rough seas!

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:16.060
That's why I need a boat.

00:16:16.060 --> 00:16:19.990
That's why I can't afford to lose!

00:16:21.440 --> 00:16:23.120
Let's battle, Yugi!

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:25.170
It's your turn!

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:29.990
Fine!  I'll also battle with all my strength!

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:32.260
Yeah!

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:33.510
Yugi.

00:16:33.940 --> 00:16:36.380
He also has problems to deal with.

00:16:36.380 --> 00:16:38.390
That was a touching story.

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:42.960
I only have 5% of the field left.

00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:45.530
I can only play one more card.

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:47.590
Here I go!

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:49.820
Giant Soldier of Stone!

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:58.160
Giant Soldier of Stone is suited for 
the remaining 5% Wasteland field.

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:01.300
Therefore, its attack and 
defense points increase.

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:03.220
That's a nice strategy.

00:17:03.220 --> 00:17:08.070
You're planning to move that monster 
into the ocean to create more land.

00:17:09.220 --> 00:17:14.450
In that case, I'll bring out more monsters 
this turn and have them all attack!

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:16.190
Great White Terror!

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:29.020
Damn!  He has Yugi cornered!

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:31.720
Your Giant Soldier of Stone is surrounded.

00:17:31.720 --> 00:17:34.600
You can't enlarge your field anymore.

00:17:34.600 --> 00:17:38.230
Too bad, Yugi.  I win.

00:17:38.230 --> 00:17:42.300
No, Kajiki.  I'll send those 
words right back to you.

00:17:42.300 --> 00:17:44.480
I was waiting for this moment.

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:45.580
What?

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:49.680
I switch Giant Soldier of 
Stone into attack position.

00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:54.420
What?

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:57.280
My monsters are underwater.

00:17:57.280 --> 00:17:59.540
You can't attack them.

00:17:59.540 --> 00:18:02.360
Who said I was going to attack your monsters?

00:18:02.780 --> 00:18:06.670
I'm attacking the card that I played.

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:10.100
The moon.

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:11.960
What?

00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:14.610
Giant Soldier of Stone, attack!

00:18:15.100 --> 00:18:17.590
Rock Crush Sword!

00:18:27.020 --> 00:18:28.590
What?

00:18:28.820 --> 00:18:31.710
The ocean is receding!

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:33.430
Why?

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:40.930
Full Moon's gravity raises the 
sea level, creating high tide.

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:48.010
When Kairyu-Shin's ability reduced the size 
of the land, Full Moon doubled that effect.

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:50.570
What?

00:18:50.570 --> 00:18:55.520
Now that Full Moon is gone, that 
effect's power is cut in half.

00:18:55.520 --> 00:18:57.450
My monsters...

00:18:57.700 --> 00:19:00.720
So I have land again.

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:04.460
Curse of Dragon!

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:10.200
I add the spell card Burning 
Land for a combo attack.

00:19:14.580 --> 00:19:16.150
Hell Flame!

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:20.430
All your monsters are destroyed.

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:23.640
I lost!

00:19:23.860 --> 00:19:26.380
He did it!  Yugi won!

00:19:26.380 --> 00:19:27.380
All right!

00:19:27.980 --> 00:19:33.020
You used your own card to 
reduce your field size.

00:19:33.490 --> 00:19:35.800
Yugi, I lose.

00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:38.200
You're great!

00:19:38.200 --> 00:19:41.550
You're quite skilled yourself.

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:47.480
I'm back down to one Star Chip.

00:19:47.480 --> 00:19:49.500
I'll have to start all over.

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:50.900
Let's both try our best!

00:19:50.900 --> 00:19:52.070
Right!

00:19:54.440 --> 00:20:00.830
Every duelist who came to this 
island has their own dreams.

00:20:03.020 --> 00:20:05.450
Before I start over, I need to eat.

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:06.870
See ya!

00:20:09.460 --> 00:20:12.300
Food!

00:20:12.300 --> 00:20:13.220
He's...

00:20:13.220 --> 00:20:15.100
...super positive.

00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:16.500
We should get going!

00:20:16.700 --> 00:20:17.700
Right!

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:19.660
I'm getting hungry.

00:20:19.660 --> 00:20:20.780
Me too.

00:20:20.780 --> 00:20:22.500
You just ate some fish!

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:25.230
Growing boys need to eat.

00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:39.200
Yugi is steadily gaining Star Chips 
when a thief suddenly appears.

00:20:39.200 --> 00:20:42.740
Yugi, you're going to accept his duel?

00:20:42.740 --> 00:20:45.800
Do you know his identity?

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:49.120
Hey!  You're Kaiba's younger brother!

00:20:49.120 --> 00:20:52.900
What's the relationship between 
Pegasus and the Kaiba brothers?

00:20:52.900 --> 00:20:56.600
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Stolen Blue-Eyes White Dragon

00:20:56.600 --> 00:20:58.530
Duel, standby!

00:21:02.660 --> 00:21:11.060
The flask glistens

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:18.910
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:19.400 --> 00:21:27.880
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:35.650
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:41.490
Shower of happiness

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:45.600
I will shower you with it

00:21:45.930 --> 00:21:53.880
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:58.110
Shower of happiness

00:21:58.380 --> 00:22:02.240
You are not alone

00:22:02.620 --> 00:22:08.960
You're protected by a 
giant ring of friendship
